    "specPath": "specs/019-dynamic-questions/spec.md",
    "status": "approved",
    "summary": "A separate, explicitly invoked class for one bounded proposition, classification, or rubric question over caller-selected context. Dynamic questions use a dedicated backend capability, structured data-only inputs, fixed request-time labels or levels, one attempt, hard cost and time limits, explicit abstention, model-derived lineage, and class-specific evaluation. They do not alter a registered plan, supply a value into a running plan, create calibration or probability by implication, invoke tools, or grant authority.\n",
    "title": "Dynamic questions as a narrow evaluated class"
  },
